-- rules/ingest.rofl — INDEXING A CORPUS, AS A PROGRAM THAT DRIVES ITSELF.
-- The caller states a goal, `must_index[code](Corpus, File)`, and this file
-- derives whether it is met, which files are missing and what to do next.
-- Nothing here parses or touches a disk; the host does, and reaches the world
-- only as facts it asserts back. A driver written as rules can be ASKED —
-- after a crash, from a snapshot, by someone who did not write the loop.
--
-- The tick is what makes it safe: `Assumption` freezes what `not p` is judged
-- against for a whole round, so a file parsed mid-round leaves the frontier
-- at the BOUNDARY, which is also the only place a volume may be lifted or
-- dropped. The status relations carry the corpus they are about, so one world
-- can hold several indexing goals, which is what a corpus split into volumes
-- looks like.

-- =========================================================================
-- INDEXED: the AST root is in the world; or the facts were cooled to disk and
-- the knowledge that they existed is not (else cooling puts the file straight
-- back on the frontier); or the scanner REFUSED it. The third arm is the one
-- that bit: when the refusal became a fact instead of a throw, the file
-- counted as parsed, emitted no `ast_file`, and the loop took the same eight
-- files every tick while reporting progress. A file the scanner has ruled on
-- is indexed, whether the ruling was a tree or a refusal.
--
-- `cooled[code](File, Path)` is written by the host after the book is on
-- disk, never before: a crash between the two costs a re-parse, the cheap
-- direction.
indexed[code](F) :- ast_file[code](_, F).

indexed[code](F) :- cooled[code](F, _).

indexed[code](F) :- ast_parse_error[code](F, _).

-- =========================================================================
-- THE GOAL. `index_complete` is a FACT a driver can stop on; `not
-- needs_index(_)` at the call site is a question whose answer depends on
-- which round asked it.
needs_index[code](C, F) :- must_index[code](C, F), not indexed[code](F).

index_incomplete[code](C) :- needs_index[code](C, _).
index_complete[code](C)   :- must_index[code](C, _),
                             not index_incomplete[code](C).

-- Identity is the tuple (Kind, Inquiry, Target): an id minted in a rule
-- changes when the rule fires twice, and nothing downstream compares across
-- ticks (rules/inquiry/intents.rofl).
candidate_intent(parse, C, F) :- needs_index[code](C, F).

-- =========================================================================
-- COOLING. A book may be cooled once indexed and nothing hot needs it.
-- `needed_hot` is empty for a pure AST index, which is why 128 volumes came
-- out self-sufficient; the day the JS model resolves across module
-- boundaries, this is the relation that stops a book being cooled under a
-- reader.
coolable[code](F) :- indexed[code](F), not needed_hot[code](F).

-- WHEN TO COOL IS A DISJUNCTION. A threshold on the join accumulator's
-- peak alone never fired over 1426 files: a pure AST index is all base facts and the join
-- accumulator stays empty while the store grows. Rows are not facts. Each
-- reason is measured by a different instrument and the host asserts whichever
-- hold; the rules decide WHAT may be cooled and never whether.
under_pressure[code](C) :- rows_pressure[code](C).
under_pressure[code](C) :- world_pressure[code](C).
under_pressure[code](C) :- memory_pressure[code](C).
under_pressure[code](C) :- volume_settled[code](C).
under_pressure[code](C) :- eviction_asked[code](C).

edb(rows_pressure).      -- the join accumulator nears `space`
edb(world_pressure).     -- the STORE nears its fact ceiling; the one that was missing
edb(memory_pressure).    -- resident memory, which only the host can see at all
edb(volume_settled).     -- the work is done and nothing pending refers to it
edb(eviction_asked).     -- a checkpoint, a shutdown, a snapshot: somebody said so

-- `must_index` leads because it binds both C and F; `coolable(F)` before
-- `under_pressure(C)` is a cross product, and rules/rule-shape.rofl counts it.
--
-- After cooling, a question about the file must REFUSE rather than answer
-- empty; `hole` is a kernel relation a rule may not conclude into, so the
-- host asserts both at the moment the book leaves memory:
--     cooled[code](File, Path).
--     hole($cold(File), cooled_to_disk).
candidate_intent(cool, C, F) :- must_index[code](C, F),
                                under_pressure[code](C),
                                coolable[code](F),
                                not cooled[code](F, _).

-- =========================================================================
-- THE CENSUS a driver prints, as sets: a count is not expressible here, so
-- the host counts and the membership stays where it can be argued with.
index_target[code](C, F) :- must_index[code](C, F).
index_left[code](C, F)   :- needs_index[code](C, F).
index_done[code](C, F)   :- must_index[code](C, F), indexed[code](F).
index_cold[code](C, F)   :- must_index[code](C, F), cooled[code](F, _).
